  /* ============================================================
     .c-button modifiers — the site's whole button semantics
     The bare .c-button is natively WHITE (--color-ui-button-bg), so the
     neutral chip above is right for it. But the network layers a modifier on
     top for every meaning, each painted from its own token, and the rule
     above flattened all of them into that same chip: the 404's only action
     and mypage's お気に入り (--primary #1b8ef3) became indistinguishable from
     a disabled control, and a destructive --delete would have read as a
     neutral one. Restore each meaning; the modifier out-specifies nothing,
     so these must come after .c-button, not before.
     EVERY modifier here is written as `.c-button.c-button--x` (0,2,0), not as a
     bare `.c-button--x` (0,1,0): the network renders half of these as
     <input type="submit"|"button">, and the generic input chip rule further down
     is (0,1,1) — it beat a bare modifier and re-flattened it. That trap already
     cost --yellow once; it was still live on yomou's イチオシレビュー filter, where
     the 検索 submit (--primary) read as a neutral chip and 全てのチェックを外す
     (--outline) as a filled one.
     ============================================================ */
  .c-button.c-button--primary {
    background-color: #1f6feb !important;
    color: #ffffff !important;
    border-color: #1f6feb !important;
  }
  /* Hover DEEPENS the blue rather than lightening it. #1f6feb already sits at
     4.6:1 under white, so the site's lighten-on-hover move would drop the
     label (and the button's icon glyph) to 3.3:1 — a hover-only contrast
     fail no load-time scan would ever see. */
  .c-button.c-button--primary:hover,
  .c-button.c-button--primary:focus,
  .c-button.c-button--primary:active {
    background-color: #1a5fd0 !important;
    color: #ffffff !important;
  }
  .c-button.c-button--delete {
    background-color: #da3633 !important;
    color: #ffffff !important;
    border-color: #da3633 !important;
  }
  /* Brand orange kept, label darkened — same treatment as the nav's
     ユーザ登録 pill (white-on-orange is 2.1:1) */
  .c-button.c-button--useradd {
    background-color: #ff922b !important;
    color: #1a1109 !important;
    border-color: #ff922b !important;
  }
  /* Natively transparent link-buttons, not filled chips.
     blog.syosetu.com ships its OWN button scale where the bare .c-button is the
     brand-blue PRIMARY and --secondary is the quiet one (white fill, --color-link
     label) — the inverse of the portal's. Our neutral chip therefore erased the
     only distinction the blog draws between its two button ranks, leaving the
     "ページの先頭へ戻る" control reading as a filled action. */
  .c-button.c-button--minor,
  .c-button.c-button--outline,
  .c-button.c-button--secondary {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    color: #5fb0e6 !important;
  }
  /* The remaining outline family carries the network's OTHER button meanings, each
     a transparent chip whose whole identity is its label colour: --outline-warn is
     the destructive one (--color-ui-theme-danger #ff6b6b), --outline-cheers the
     なろうチアーズ brand green (#0ca678, matched with --primary-cheers' #12b886
     fill), --outline-none-active the disabled twin of --outline. Filling all four
     with the neutral chip made danger, brand and disabled read identically. */
  .c-button.c-button--outline-warn {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    color: #ff7b72 !important;
  }
  .c-button.c-button--outline-cheers {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    color: #3fbf95 !important;
  }
  .c-button.c-button--primary-cheers {
    background-color: #12b886 !important;
    color: #04231a !important;
    border-color: #12b886 !important;
  }
  .c-button.c-button--outline-none-active {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    color: #7d8590 !important;
  }
  /* The "already done" state (e.g. already favourited) — must read inactive */
  .c-button.c-button--none-active {
    background-color: #30363d !important;
    color: #8b949e !important;
    border-color: #30363d !important;
  }
  /* The impression/feedback form's 送信[確認] submit is natively a pale-yellow
     CTA (cream #fffcde fill, gold #fcd27e border) — the site's "confirm" accent,
     distinct from the blue --primary. The base .c-button rule flattened it to the
     neutral chip, so the form's primary action stopped reading as one. Keep the
     yellow identity as a warm gold fill with dark text. The submit is an
     <input type="submit">, so the generic `input[type="submit"]` chip rule
     (0,1,1) out-specifies a bare `.c-button--yellow` (0,1,0) — qualify with the
     base class (0,2,0) so the modifier wins, same trap as .c-under-nav__pdflink. */
  .c-button.c-button--yellow {
    background-color: #d6a44a !important;
    color: #1a1109 !important;
    border-color: #d6a44a !important;
  }
  .c-button.c-button--yellow:hover,
  .c-button.c-button--yellow:focus,
  .c-button.c-button--yellow:active {
    background-color: #c4933b !important;
    color: #1a1109 !important;
  }

  /* Rating stars / point form */
