     yomou's #trad results. The synopsis under them is a #663333 maroon. */
  article.search_novel h1 a {
    color: #f0954a !important;
  }
  article.search_novel h1 a:hover {
    color: #ffb877 !important;
  }
  article.search_novel p.ex {
    color: #b6c0ca !important;
  }
  /* The rating panel beside each hit is fill-less: its #66cc99 green frame is
     the whole box, matching the 総合ポイント figure inside it. The blanket border
     reset flattened all 20 a page to the divider grey. */
  p.point {
    border-color: #66cc99 !important;
  }
  /* noc's ranking explainer heading is a #aa3366 wine that drops to 2.4:1, and
     each BEST5 block's own head is the legacy #663300 brown at 1.5:1 */
  #ranking_about h3,
  .h2_rank {
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  /* The period tabs above each ranking are pale pills (#ffeeff on noc, #eeffff
     on mnlt) with BLACK labels, and the current one is a white pill whose only
     other marker is a 2px bottom rule in the site's brand hue — which the
     blanket border reset flattened. Rebuild the scale and restore each site's
     own accent on its own selector. `.change_rank` is the switch-to-the-other-
     ranking pill, natively the loudest chip in the row. */
  #ranking_navi a,
  .r_navilist li,
  .r_navilist li a {
    background-color: #161b22 !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  #ranking_navi li.on a,
  .r_navilist li.on,
  .r_navilist li.on a {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  #ranking_navi li.change_rank a,
  .r_navilist li.change_rank,
  .r_navilist li.change_rank a {
    background-color: #3a2f14 !important;
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  #ranking_navi li.on a,
  #ranking_navi a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: #ffaaff !important;
  }
  .r_navilist li.on,
  .r_navilist a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: #66ccff !important;
  }
  /* The ユーザ登録 CTA on サイト概要 is a pale plate — #eeccee on noc, #ddeeee on
     mnlt — carrying a link label that our accent blue leaves at ~2:1 on it. */
  a.entry_link {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #9bd4ff !important;
  }
  /* mid's PHONE sheet paints the bare tag — `article { background-color:#fff }` —
     so its review list, search results, ranking and 閲覧履歴 all render as white
     slabs no class-scoped rule can reach; the 閲覧履歴 panels add their own #fff
     h2/h3/div plus an #eee radial-gradient wrapper. `article` is (0,0,1), below
     every class rule in this sheet, so the elevated cards above keep their fill;
     on the main network every <article> (the reader's .p-novel, the blog's
     .c-article) is natively bare, so clearing it changes nothing there. */
  article,
  .order_box,
  .review_list h1,
  .rireki_setting,
  .rireki_setting h2,
  .rireki_setting h3,
  .rireki_setting div {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    background-image: none !important;
  }
  /* ...and the history page's controls are #eee / #f9fcff chips */
  .rireki_box a,
  a#rireki_alldelete,
  a#disable_history,
  a#enable_history {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
  }
  /* The MAIN network's 閲覧履歴 (yomou.syosetu.com/rireki/list/) now renders the
     same two ids as modern `.c-button--primary` CTAs. The id rule above is
     (1,0,1) and beat the modifier (0,2,0), so 閲覧履歴を記録しない and
     閲覧履歴をすべて削除する sat as neutral chips beside a 続きから読む that
     carries the identical classes and paints blue. Qualify to (1,1,1). */
  a#rireki_alldelete.c-button--primary,
  a#disable_history.c-button--primary,
  a#enable_history.c-button--primary {
    background-color: #1f6feb !important;
    border-color: #1f6feb !important;
    color: #ffffff !important;
  }
  /* With those panels dark, everything written on them turns out to be the same
     legacy #333/#444/#555 ink the R18 base sheets set directly. */
  .review_list .novelinfo,
  .review_list .review,
  .rireki_setting p,
  .rireki_setting div {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  .rireki_setting h2,
  .rireki_setting h3,
  h2.rank {
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  a#rireki_alldelete span,
  a#disable_history span,
  a#enable_history span {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }

  /* ミッドナイトノベルズ (mid) is a FOURTH frontend: its chrome is natively dark
     (black header, neon-green sprites, all fine on our base) but the entire content
     column is one white <main>, with a #ccc sub-nav strip above it and a white
     pagetop/ad rail below. Our light body text sat on all of it. <main> is bare
     everywhere else on the network (reader, novelcom, blog all compute transparent),
     so clearing it is a no-op off mid. The #666 work-type / note copy inside goes
     dark-on-dark once the panel darkens. */
  main,
  .header_news,
  .koukoku,
  .pagetop {
    background-color: transparent !important;
  }
  .header_info {
    background-color: #0d1117 !important;
  }
  .note_box,
  .info_box,
  span.type {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* mid's ranking/list nav rows hover into a `background:` shorthand gradient
     (#fdfdfd → #f0f0f0, with an #edffed stop on the -ms branch) — a full-width
     WHITE bar carrying the row's own light-blue label at ~1.4:1, and the only
     hover cue the page has. A background-COLOR override paints behind the
     gradient, so the image has to go. Both selectors are one rule in the site's
     sheet. */
  nav.ranklist_nav li a:hover,
  nav.list_link li a:hover {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    background-image: none !important;
  }
  /* mid's ranking pages list every entry as a <dl class="ranking"> whose <dd>
     carries the 作者 line at #666 — 5.7:1 on the site's white page, 3.1:1 on
     ours, and the dimmest thing in a 25-row list. The title and 作品情報 inside
     it are anchors and keep their own colour. `dl.ranking` exists nowhere else
     on the network (verified across the portal, yomou, noc, mnlt and mid's own
     top), so the bare selector stays mid-only. */
  dl.ranking dd {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }

  /* The R18 paged ranking LIST (/rank/list/type/<period>/) is a different
     container family from the ranking TOP handled above. noc wraps its 300 rows
     in a `.ranking_inbox` painted a solid #ffffff — a full-length white slab
     carrying our light body text; mnlt's is bare and mid has none. Each row's
     heading is `#rank_box .rank_h` with a `.name` author span, both left at the
     base sheet's universal `* { color:#333 }` — a DIRECT match, so no inherited
     body colour reaches them. The title inside is an anchor and keeps its own. */
  .ranking_inbox {
    background-color: transparent !important;
  }
  #rank_box .rank_h,
  #rank_box .rank_h .ranking_number {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  #rank_box .rank_h .name {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* The 総合/短編/連載中/完結済 novel-type chips are the class twin of the
     .r_navilist period pills above: a pale plate (#ffeeff on noc, #eeffff on
     mnlt) under a BLACK label, the current one marked only by a 2px rule in the
     site's own accent that the blanket border reset flattened. noc wraps the row
     in `.r_navititle` (class), mnlt in `#r_navititle` (id) — that pair is the
     only way to tell the two hosts apart from CSS. */
  ul.r_noveltypelist li,
  ul.r_noveltypelist li a {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  ul.r_noveltypelist li.on,
  ul.r_noveltypelist li.on a {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  ul.r_noveltypelist a:hover {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
  }
  .r_navititle ul.r_noveltypelist li.on {
    border-bottom-color: #ffaaff !important;
  }
  #r_navititle ul.r_noveltypelist li.on {
    border-bottom-color: #66ccff !important;
  }
  /* mid's paged ranking list is a THIRD family again: each of its 300 rows is a
     #fcfcfc `.rankList_info` card, and `.rankList` ships a #666 ink that the
     作者 / 連載中 / キーワード / 最終更新日 lines inherit. The rank and point
     figures keep their own #3bd cyan (a direct declaration beats inheritance). */
  .rankList_info {
    background-color: transparent !important;
  }
  .rankList {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  /* mid marks the current period tab and novel-type chip with a #008877 teal
     rule plus label — 2.2:1 on our base, and the label is additionally
     overwritten by the generic link blue, so selected and unselected render
     identical. Lift the teal on both; it is the row's only "you are here" cue. */
  nav.rank_navtype li.on,
  ul.rank_noveltypelist li.on {
    border-bottom-color: #3ac9b4 !important;
  }
  nav.rank_navtype li.on a,
  ul.rank_noveltypelist li.on a {
    color: #3ac9b4 !important;
  }
  /* mid's 総合ポイント figure is the green counterpart of noc's red .attention —
     the emphasised number on every search row. Its #228855 clears 4.5:1 on mid's
     own near-white card but only reaches 4.0:1 on our base, so shift it up the
     same green the チアーズ text uses and keep the emphasis. */
  span.globalpoint,
  span.globalpoint .number {
    color: #3fbf95 !important;
  }
  /* mid's section lead paragraph is a #777 grey tuned for its white content
     column; on our base it drops under 4:1. */
  p.contents_description {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }

  /* The R18 group serves its OWN phone sheets (smp_base / smp_noc / the mnlt and mid
     equivalents) — a fifth family none of the desktop selectors above touch, and one
     the desktop viewport can never render. Everything here is a full-width band or a
     chip in that family: the "»see all" footer bar (.a_line, a white gradient), the
     bare section heads directly under <body> (a near-white pink/grey band with #333
     or #663300 text), the beginner/ranking/blog list chips (pale pink, cream and
     white gradients), the keyword pills, mnlt's pale-blue #navi bar and mid's white
     article. `body > h2` and #navi exist ONLY here — every other page type on the
     network, desktop and phone, has zero of both. */
  div#navi,
  div.a_line,
  article.top_0,
  ul.top_listlink li,
  ul.top_mainkeyword a,
  div.beginner li,
  div.beginner_rank li,
  div.beginner_type li,
  h2.official-x_headline {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    background-image: none !important;
  }
  /* Clearing those plates leaves the 新着一覧 / ランキング pair identical: their
     only remaining difference was ランキング's saturated #ee9933 frame + #ee7633
     label, both flattened. (新着一覧's own frame is a pale #cc99bb on noc /
     #99bbcc on mnlt — correctly left flattened.) */
  div.beginner li.ranking,
  div.beginner_rank li.ranking {
    border-color: #ee9933 !important;
  }
  div.beginner li.ranking a,
  div.beginner_rank li.ranking a {
    color: #f0954a !important;
  }
  /* Keep the heads' background-IMAGE: on these h2s it is the section icon
     (news.gif megaphone, book.gif), not a band — the band is the colour. */
  body > h2 {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  p.outlink,
  ul.link_list > li {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* The R18 phone SUB-pages (rankings, search results, サイト概要) add a second
     tier of the same family: a `body > h3` section band (white on サイト概要, a
     #333 head above each BEST5 block), the ranking's period pills as
     `ul#r_navilist` — a white strip of pale pink / pale cyan chips, the id twin
     of the desktop `.r_navilist` handled above — the ユーザ登録 CTA as a white
     gradient, and, on every one of the 20 hits per results page, an
     `▼あらすじ等` disclosure bar at #f3f9f9. Only the phone sheets emit any of
     these. */
  body > h3 {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  ul#r_navilist,
  ul#r_navilist > li {
    background-color: #161b22 !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  ul#r_navilist > li.on {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  /* …and beside it the novel-type row as `ul#r_noveltypelist`, the id twin of
     the desktop `ul.r_noveltypelist` above: four solid-white chips (#ffffff on
     noc, #f0ffff on mnlt) under a #006699 label, the current one #eeeeee with a
     #999999 rule. These legacy R18 rows always come in a desktop-class /
     phone-id pair — fix the twin whenever you fix one. */
  ul#r_noveltypelist > li,
  ul#r_noveltypelist > li a {
    background-color: #161b22 !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  ul#r_noveltypelist > li.on,
  ul#r_noveltypelist > li.on a {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  ul#r_noveltypelist > li.on {
    border-bottom-color: #8b949e !important;
  }
  /* Ranks 1–5 are medal GIFs; 6位 down is a text `.ranking_number` the phone
     sheet paints #993333 — a maroon that reads on the site's white page and
     vanishes on ours. Keep it in the native red family. The keyword and date
     lines under each row are the same sheet's #666666. */
  ul.ranking li .ranking_number {
    color: #ff7b72 !important;
  }
  ul.ranking li.keyword,
  ul.ranking li.date {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* mid's phone sheet moves the #666 ink off `.rankList` onto `.rankList p`
     directly, so lifting the container is not enough — the 作者 / 連載中 /
     キーワード / 最終更新日 paragraphs stay dark. Re-assert the rank line's own
     #33bbdd afterwards; the broad lift would otherwise swallow it. */
  .rankList p {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  .rankList p.rank {
    color: #33bbdd !important;
  }
  /* mid's phone results pager drops the <a> on the page you are on and leaves a
     bare <span>, which the R18 base sheet's universal `* { color:#333 }` then
     matches DIRECTLY — 1.4:1, beside ten bright blue page links, so the one
     number that carries state is the only one you cannot read. */
  .pager-search span {
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  div#entry_link > a,
  .genre_list.content-bg,
  .toggle-next-tab {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    background-image: none !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  ul.novellist li.date,
  div.update24 {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* mnlt's ジャンル選択 head inside that panel is a #682485 purple at 1.6:1 */
  .genre_list .content-head_h3 {
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     Tables (generic), toasts, announcements
     ============================================================ */
  table,
  th,
  td {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
    border-color: #2d333b !important;
  }
  th {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
  }

  .c-toast,
  .c-toast__box-right {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
    color: #e6edf3 !important;
    border-color: #2d333b !important;
  }
  .c-announce,
  .c-announce--note {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
    border-color: #2d333b !important;
  }
  /* The emphasis span is the reader's CONTENT WARNING — <R15>, 〔残酷描写〕,
     the age gate — painted #dd0000 by the site. It used to inherit the box's
     body colour above and read as ordinary prose. Warm red keeps the warning
     legible AND alarming. Anchors with the same class stay link-blue via
     .c-announce a, which out-specifies this. */
  .c-announce__emphasis {
    color: #ff7b72 !important;
  }
  .c-announce a,
  .c-announce--note a,
  .help-link {
    color: #5fb0e6 !important;
  }

  /* Hovering a 関連作品 title paints a cream --color-recommend-title-bg (#ffe)
     bar the full width of the list and darkens the label to #000 — on dark that
     is a white strip carrying our accent blue at ~1.7:1, and it is the list's
     only pointer feedback. The token is defined only on the reader/index pages,
     and the row exists only under the pointer, so no load-time scan reaches it. */
  .p-recommend__title-link:hover {
    background-color: #2d333b !important;
  }

  /* Recommendation "NNNNN user" bookmark-count badge — was green text
     on a pale green pill; keep the green meaning on a dark chip */
  .p-recommend__info-item--bookmarked {
    background-color: #15291f !important;
    color: #56d364 !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     User / author page (mypage.syosetu.com)
     ============================================================ */
  /* The profile header ships a solid white banner — it hides the
     display name (already light) and its block/mute + tab links.
     Neutralize the banner so everything on it reads on dark. */
  .p-userheader,
  .p-userheader__body,
  .p-userheader__tab {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    border-color: #262c33 !important;
  }
  .p-userheader__username {
    color: #e6edf3 !important;
  }
  .p-userheader__username-info {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* The generic c-link component (activity-report / series / bookmark
     titles) renders mid-to-dark blue (#1b8ef3 / #1864ab); the --lg size
     is dark-on-dark. Lift the whole component to the readable accent. */
  .c-link,
  .c-link--md,
  .c-link--lg {
    color: #5fb0e6 !important;
  }
  .c-link:hover,
  .c-link--md:hover,
  .c-link--lg:hover {
    color: #9bd4ff !important;
  }
  /* c-panel list rows highlight on hover with a translucent light wash
     (rgba(241,243,245,.5)) that turns into a grey glare block on dark —
     swap it for a subtle dark elevated hover. */
  .c-panel__list-item:hover {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
  }
  /* The レビュー作品 tag (.c-label--review) is a light #e9ecef pill whose label
     inherits our body colour — light-on-light, glaring and unreadable. Darken it
     to an elevated chip; the sibling filled badges (連載 pink --long, 短編 blue
     --short) keep their own brand fills. */
  .c-label--review {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  /* The UNMODIFIED .c-label is the same trap one level up: its base rule is
     `color:var(--color-text) (#333); background:var(--color-label-theme-default)
     (#e9ecef)`, and yomou's イチオシレビュー list uses exactly that bare form for its
     レビュー作品 tag — ten light chips glaring down the page. Every coloured sibling
     redeclares BOTH properties, so a flat `.c-label{color}` would out-!important
     their white labels; scope the two tokens to the component instead and only the
     unmodified chip moves. --long is the one exception: it declares a pink fill but
     NO colour, so it rides --color-text and needs its dark label re-asserted. */
  .c-label {
    --color-text: #c4cdd6 !important;
    --color-label-theme-default: #21262d !important;
  }
  .c-label--long {
    color: #1a1109 !important;
  }
  /* The 代表作 badge (.c-label--masterpiece) is the lone OUTLINE label — a
     transparent chip whose identity is its green #0ca678 border + matching
     text, not a fill. The blanket `* { border-color }` reset flattened the
     border to the dark divider grey, so beside the crisp filled pink/blue
     status pills it read as an unframed floating label. Restore the green
     edge (the text is already green) so the outlined chip reads again. */
  .c-label--masterpiece {
    border-color: #0ca678 !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     Footer
     ============================================================ */
  .l-footer,
  .l-foot-contents,
  footer {
    background-color: #0d1117 !important;
    color: #b6c0ca !important;
    border-color: #262c33 !important;
  }
  /* The mypage/group footer (.p-footer) ships a brand TEAL nav band and a
     bright CYAN copyright bar (audit-blind: colored, not near-white) —
     neutralize both onto the footer dark so they don't glare. The portal
     footer carries the same cyan band as a standalone .p-copyright strip.
     On blog.syosetu.com there is no __foot child at all: .p-footer IS the
     copyright bar, so the cyan landed on the wrapper and the whole strip
     across the bottom of the blog stayed brand cyan. Name the wrapper too. */
  .p-footer,
  .p-footer__body,
  .p-footer__foot,
  .p-copyright {
    background-color: #0d1117 !important;
  }
  .p-footer__foot,
  .p-copyright {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  .l-footer a,
  .l-foot-contents a,
  footer a,
  .p-footer a {
    color: #9bd4ff !important;
  }

  /* Footer ranking-tag block / its "cannot display" notice are bare #444
     dark-on-dark in the foot-contents — lift to muted grey */
  .p-rankingtag,
  .p-rankingtag__notice,
  .p-rankingtag__item {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* On R18 (novel18) readers authors embed a 書籍化 book-promo into the
     footer .p-rankingtag slot as inline-styled HTML — light #fff / #C7FBC7
     wrapper <div>s carrying #333 text that glare as a big bright panel on
     the dark reader. Neutralize the inline light fills and lift the inherited
     text; the Amazon/FANZA <a> buttons keep their brand red/blue and the
     book-cover <img> is untouched. */
  .p-rankingtag div {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  /* The same authors put their headings and body copy in <h3>/<p>/<span> with an
     inline colour of their own — an inline declaration on the element beats the
     wrapper's lifted ink, so once the light paper below it is neutralized those
     near-black maroons sit on the dark footer at ~1.1:1. <a> is deliberately
     absent: the Amazon / FANZA / support-site buttons keep their brand hues. */
  .p-rankingtag div h1,
  .p-rankingtag div h2,
  .p-rankingtag div h3,
  .p-rankingtag div h4,
  .p-rankingtag div h5,
  .p-rankingtag div h6,
  .p-rankingtag div p,
  .p-rankingtag div span,
  .p-rankingtag div li,
  .p-rankingtag div td,
  .p-rankingtag div b,
  .p-rankingtag div strong,
  .p-rankingtag div small,
  .p-rankingtag div font {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }

  /* SNS share buttons - keep brand fills but ensure text legible.
     On the reader and story index the row sits inside .l-foot-contents, whose
     `a` rule (0,1,1) out-specifies a bare .c-sns__button (0,1,0) and repainted
     the LINE button's white label footer-link blue on its brand green — qualify
     through the item wrapper (0,2,0) so the label wins wherever the row lands. */
  .c-sns__item .c-sns__button {
    color: #e6edf3 !important;
  }

  /* R18 age-confirmation interstitial (年齢確認, the noc/mnlt/mid gate):
     a bare #modal whose heading (#444/#333) and body copy (#000) are
     dark-on-dark and all but invisible. Lift headings to amber and copy
     to body text; the Enter / exit links stay blue. */
  #modal h1,
  #modal h2 {
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  #modal,
  #modal p {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  /* nl.syosetu.com/redirect/ageauth/ — the gate every noc / mnlt / mid visitor
     lands on first, desktop AND phone. Its two choices are fill-less boxes
     whose `3px double` edge is their whole identity: cyan #18b7cd for "under
     18, leave" and pink #eeaae0 for "18+, enter". The blanket border reset
     crushed both to the divider grey, so the only control on the page read as
     two identical unlabelled frames. Same class as the #index_* gates below. */
  #modal .no {
    border-color: #18b7cd !important;
  }
  #modal .yes {
    border-color: #eeaae0 !important;
  }
  /* ...but #modal is only ONE of the group's age gates. Each R18 site serves a
     different gate markup, and it is the FIRST page every visitor to noc / mnlt
     sees, so none of it is reachable behind a login: ノクターン's desktop gate is
     one solid #fff page (#index_contents wrapping a #fcfbfc 【利用上の注意】 box,
     over a #fff #index_footer), and both phone gates paint the same box's <h2> a
     full-width #fff band, with ムーンライト adding a near-white #f5f5ff title
     plate. Neutralize every plate; #index_title keeps its logo GIF, since only
     the colour behind it is the band. */
  #index_contents,
  #index_footer,
  #index_attention,
  #index_attention > h2,
  h1#index_title {
    background-color: transparent !important;
  }
  /* The 【利用上の注意】 heading is 16px bold #cc3399 on the phone sheet — 3.8:1
     once its white plate is gone. The desktop gate paints the same heading the
     network's brighter #ff3399 (5.3:1), so adopt that everywhere. */
  #index_attention > h2 {
    color: #ff3399 !important;
  }
  /* With the plate dark, every line on the gate turns out to be legacy #333 —
     and NOT by inheritance: both R18 base sheets declare a universal
     `* { color:#333 }`, and a direct match beats anything cascading down from
     our `body`, so `body { color }` never reaches one of them. Name the gate's
     own boxes. */
  #index_contents,
  #index_contents p,
  #index_contents div,
  #index_attention,
  #index_mnlt,
  #index_mid,
  #no_yes,
  .entrance_text,
  .entrance_text p {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  /* Every framed box on the gate is fill-less: its coloured edge IS the box.
     The blanket border reset above flattened them all to the divider grey,
     leaving the notice and the sister-site cards as unframed text. Restore the
     native edge per box. The desktop and phone sheets use different shades for
     two of them, so the desktop values are qualified with #index_contents,
     which exists only on the desktop gate. */
  #index_attention {
    border-color: #cc3399 !important;
  }
  #index_contents #index_attention {
    border-color: #cc99ff !important;
  }
  #entrance_in {
    border-top-color: #aa99ff !important;
    border-bottom-color: #aa99ff !important;
  }
  #index_mnlt {
    border-color: #3399cc !important;
  }
  #index_contents #index_mnlt {
    border-color: #66ccff !important;
  }
  #index_noc {
    border-color: #cc3399 !important;
  }
  #index_mid {
    border-color: #00dd99 !important;
  }
  /* The gate's NO / YES pair is the only control on the page. The phone sheet
     makes them solid teal #44afaa / magenta #d449a9 chips and paints the label
     white at `#entrance a` (0,1,1) — our generic `a` rule wins that on
     !important alone and dropped both labels, and their sub-caption, to the
     accent blue at ~1.8:1 on the fill. Pin them back to white. Scoped by the
     phone-only ids so the desktop gate's bare links keep the accent blue. */
  #entrance a#no,
  #entrance a#yes,
  #entrance a#no span,
  #entrance a#yes span {
    color: #ffffff !important;
  }
  /* ムーンライト's desktop gate is a fourth layout again, and all of its copy is
     legacy-dark: the lead is #0066aa (2.6:1) and the notice #666 (3.0:1). Worse,
     mnlt's legacy base sheet ships a universal `* { color:#333 }` — a DIRECT
     match, which beats anything the <a> above it inherits down — so the caption
     under each entry link ("入場します。") rendered #333 at 1.4:1, i.e. invisible.
     Name them explicitly; the entry links themselves stay accent blue. */
  #index_right p.index_text {
    color: #9bd4ff !important;
  }
  p.index_attention,
  .free,
  .no_free {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* That same gate hangs its 890x860 wordmark off #container as a raster
     background — a solid WHITE plate filling the left half of the page — and
     rules the entry links with two opaque white PNGs. No colour rule reaches
     either. An INSET box-shadow paints over an element's background but under
     its content, so it veils the plate without restating the image URL (a
     re-declared background-image would land the moon logo on every other
     #container in the group, none of which has one); the PNGs invert the way
     the reader's 挿絵 pill does. */
  div#container {
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 9999px rgba(20, 24, 29, 0.94) !important;
  }
  img[src*="mnlt_index_entrance_line"] {
    filter: invert(0.92) hue-rotate(180deg);
  }
  /* ムーンライト is the one R18 site whose header WORDMARK is an opaque plate:
     both mnlt_titlelogo.gif (desktop) and mnltk_logo.gif (phone) bake a #f3f3f3
     background into the pixels, so the mark ships as a bright rectangle in the
     dark header of every mnlt page. No element-bg scan sees it — it is an <img>.
     Its ink is PASTEL (pink wordmark, cyan crescent), so a partial invert leaves
     the plate visible; a full invert lands it on rgb(20,13,28) — within a few
     units of the #0d1117 header — and hue-rotate restores both brand hues.
     ノクターン's and ミッドナイト's own wordmarks are already dark; leave them. */
  img[src*="mnlt_titlelogo"],
  img[src*="mnltk_logo"] {
    filter: invert(1) hue-rotate(180deg) !important;
  }

  /* Ad / PR slots: neutral dark so blank slots don't flash white */
  .c-ad,
  .c-ad__item-horizontal,
  .c-pr {
    background-color: transparent !important;
  }
  /* The "PR" label is the ad DISCLOSURE — it must stay readable. Its own ink is
     rgba(73,80,87,.5), a half-transparent dark grey that composites to a legible
     mid-grey on the site's light body and to near-invisible on ours. Opaque so
     the alpha cannot re-darken it against the page base. */
  .c-pr {
    color: #8b949e !important;
  }
  /* The floating "flexible sticky" ad's close button is an inline SVG whose
     polygon carries style="fill:#000;stroke:#000" — a pure-black X. It sits on
     the ad's own light creative natively, but on our dark page it renders as a
     black-on-dark X floating over the ranking rows: the ad's only dismiss
     control, unusable. Both audits are blind to it (SVG paint, and only WHITE
     fills are flagged). Repaint the glyph light and back it with a dark chip so
     it also reads if a light creative loads behind it. The mobile sheet serves the
     same control under a DIFFERENT id (#flexible-sticky-wiped-button) with the same
     inline black polygon, so the desktop-only id left the SP dismiss unusable. */
  /* A THIRD sticky-ad network (Geniee) serves the same dismiss under
     #geniee_overlay_close — same 512-viewBox polygon with inline
     style="fill:#000;stroke:#000". Its own bg is transparent, so leave the
     chip off and repaint the glyph only. */
  #flexible-sticky-ov-close-button,
  #flexible-sticky-wiped-button {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
  }
  #flexible-sticky-ov-close-button svg polygon,
  #flexible-sticky-ov-close-button svg path,
  #flexible-sticky-wiped-button svg polygon,
  #flexible-sticky-wiped-button svg path,
  #geniee_overlay_close svg polygon,
  #geniee_overlay_close svg path {
    fill: #c4cdd6 !important;
    stroke: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     なろうデベロッパー (dev.syosetu.com)
     A frontend of its own under the same domain — the technical manuals,
     the API / Atom references and the widget guide — built on a token set
     that exists NOWHERE else: every name below is undefined on the portal,
     yomou, mypage, the reader, novelcom, the blog and all three R18 hosts,
     so remapping them at :root lands on dev alone. They paint the
     full-height #f1f3f5 nav column, the #f8f9fa document/notice boxes, the
     mint #e6fcf5 tips callouts and the #f1f3f5 / #e8ebef inline-code chips
     — thirty of those on a single manual page. --color-accent (the cyan
     bullet + heading rule) and --color-button-primaly already read on dark
     and stay.
     ============================================================ */
  :root {
    --color-gnav-bg: #0d1117 !important;
    --color-box-bg: #1c2128 !important;
    --color-code-bg: #21262d !important;
    --color-tips-bg: #16241f !important;
    --color-tips-inline-bg: #2b3138 !important;
    --color-site-tips: #16241f !important;
    /* the manuals' warning box paints its label AND its edge from this one */
    --color-site-notice: #ff7b72 !important;
  }
  /* ...but that box is fill-less, so the edge IS the box, and the blanket
     border reset crushes it to the divider grey ahead of the token. */
  .c-attention {
    border-color: #ff7b72 !important;
  }
  /* The two manual cards on the dev top are white plates painted from
     --color-site-base, which the rest of the network also consumes, so they
     take a selector instead. Their body copy is the #343a40 --color-site-text
     declared on the anchor itself, so it needs lifting with the fill. */
  .p-index-nav__item a {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  /* Each card's icon is a PNG whose document silhouette is drawn in the same
     #343a40 as the copy — 1.4:1 once the plate behind it is dark, i.e. only
     the coloured gear survives. Inverting restores the outline; hue-rotate
     keeps the gear on its own brand hue (cyan for 技術マニュアル, pink for R18)
     instead of the complement a bare inversion produces. */
  .p-index-nav__item-icon img {
    filter: invert(1) hue-rotate(180deg);
  }
  /* The インラインサーチ widget (dev.syosetu.com/nish/sh/, embedded as an
     <iframe> four times on its own manual page and on any site that uses it)
     is a bare document whose only chrome is a #fff attribution bar. It exists
     only inside that frame — `#narou` and `.novel_list` match zero elements on
     every other page of the network. */
  #narou {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
    border-bottom-color: rgba(24, 183, 205, 0.5) !important;
  }
  /* Every dev section heading is marked by a 2px cyan border-left and nothing
     else; the blanket border reset flattened it to the divider grey. */
  .c-title--md {
    border-left-color: #18b7cd !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     Error / 404 page (syosetu.com/<bad-url>)
     A full-width solid #fff panel; its teal #0d6572 heading would go
     dark-on-dark once the panel darkens, so lift it to the page amber.
     ============================================================ */
  .p-error-panel {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  .p-error-panel__heading {
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  .p-error-panel__support-text {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     Mobile (SP) frontend
     The network serves a separate stylesheet family to phone user agents
     (base_narou-sp.css / p_novel-sp.css / p_index-sp.css). It reuses most of the
     desktop component classes, so the rules above already carry it — but a handful
     of surfaces exist ONLY there, painted from SP-only tokens, and each renders as
     a full-width bright band across an otherwise dark page. None of these elements
     is present in the desktop DOM, so the plain selectors below cannot reach it;
     the two that ARE shared are remapped through their token instead (see :root
     block at the end of this section).
     ============================================================ */
  /* The reader / 作品情報 / 感想一覧 secondary menu row (作品情報・感想・レビュー) sits
     under the sticky header at --color-bg-menu-sp #f6f6f6 — a white strip carrying
     our light labels. */
  .c-menu__second {
    background-color: #161b22 !important;
  }
  /* The SP header's ログイン link bullets itself with a 16x16 login.gif — an OPAQUE
     (no alpha) raster tile of a grey key on WHITE, so it renders as a bright chip
     against the dark header bar at the very top of every SP page. Same class as the
     desktop help.gif: it cannot be recoloured, so swap in a key drawn in the link's
     own accent blue and pin every background component (the site's shorthand leaves
     background-size at `auto`, which would resolve against the SVG's 512 viewBox). */
  .c-menu__first-item--login::before {
    background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf8,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 512 512'%3E%3Cpath fill='%235fb0e6' d='M336 352c97.2 0 176-78.8 176-176S433.2 0 336 0S160 78.8 160 176c0 18.7 2.9 36.8 8.3 53.7L7 391c-4.5 4.5-7 10.6-7 17v80c0 13.3 10.7 24 24 24h80c13.3 0 24-10.7 24-24v-40h40c13.3 0 24-10.7 24-24v-40h40c6.4 0 12.5-2.5 17-7l33.3-33.3c16.9 5.4 35 8.3 53.7 8.3zM376 96a40 40 0 1 1 0 80 40 40 0 0 1 0-80z'/%3E%3C/svg%3E") !important;
    background-repeat: no-repeat !important;
    background-position: center center !important;
    background-size: 16px 16px !important;
  }
  /* The chapter's 感想を書く disclosure bar (--color-impression-toggle-sp #fcfcfc)
     is a full-width near-white band; its label inherits our light body colour and
     disappears into it. */
  .c-novel-feedback-form__open-imp {
    background-color: #161b22 !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  /* The bookmark bar's ▼感想を書く chip is a pale-blue --color-bg-to-impr-button
     #edf2ff pill whose blue label reads ~2:1 on it. */
  .p-bookmark-bar__bkm-link--sp-honbun {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #9bd4ff !important;
  }
  /* The drawer's 閉じる bar and the footer's ページトップへ bar are both a solid
     brand-cyan #18b7cd strip — the two brightest things on any SP page — with a
     link on them that our accent blue leaves at ~2:1. */
  .p-drawer-nav__close a,
  .p-footer__pagetop a {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #9bd4ff !important;
  }
  /* yomou's ランキング一覧 drawer trigger is a light --color-ui-bg--tapable #e2e6ea
     bar; keep the Narou orange label but lift it for the dark chip. */
  .c-control__bar {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #f0954a !important;
  }
  /* The legacy SP search builder stacks four pale-blue #c8dfee condition toggles
     (ジャンル選択 / 詳細条件設定 / 検索ワードを選択 / 除外ワードを選択) and two pure-white
     #fff link-section headings (検索 / 一覧). The 履歴から検索 sibling is already the
     neutral chip via the generic button rule — match it. */
  .search_toggle.list_menu {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  h3.menu_list {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  /* The SP search RESULTS are a fourth result family (#accordion .smpnovel_list
     accordions, plus a #trad > .section header and a .page_bar pager). Every one of
     them declares the legacy #333 on itself, so the `#trad` lift further up never
     reaches them: the searched keyword, the result count, every 作者 / 連載中 /
     ジャンル line, the synopsis, the Nコード/キーワード block and the current-page
     marker all rendered as a near-invisible smudge, with only the orange titles and
     blue links showing. Titles and links carry their own colour and stay as they are. */
  #trad > .section,
  #trad > .page_bar {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  #trad > .section > p.bb {
    color: #e6c9a8 !important;
  }
  #trad > .page_bar b {
    color: #e6edf3 !important;
  }
  #trad > .attenstion_koushin,
  #accordion .accordion_head,
  #accordion .smpnovel_ex,
  #accordion .smpnovel_list p {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* Each expanded card's この作品を読む CTA keeps a mid-teal gradient that leaves our
     accent-blue label at ~2.3:1 — give it the same elevated chip the desktop
     この作品を読む button gets. The fill is a `background:` gradient, so a
     background-COLOR override alone paints behind it and changes nothing. */
  #accordion .read_button {
    background: #21262d !important;
    background-image: none !important;
    color: #e6edf3 !important;
    border-color: #2d333b !important;
  }
  /* Two SP surfaces share a class with a desktop element that is styled
     differently, so a plain selector would repaint the desktop one too: the drawer
     section headings (.c-navlist__headline — bare text in the desktop footer, an
     #eef5f6 band in the SP drawer) and the 表示調整 section headers
     (.p-adjust-layout__title — bare on desktop, an #eef3ff band on SP). Both bands
     are painted from a token no desktop rule consumes, so remap the token: the fix
     lands on SP only. */
  :root {
    --color-ui-c-drawer-headline-bg: #21262d !important;
    --color-adjust-layout-bg-title: #21262d !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     Google Funding Choices consent dialog (.fc-consent-root)
     Rendered in the MAIN document on first visit — a solid white
     modal flashing over the dark page. Darken the panels and dividers;
     the blue CTA buttons keep their brand fill.
     ============================================================ */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog-content,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog-header,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-faq-contents,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-faq-icon,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-preference-container {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
  }
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog-headline,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-header-text,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog p,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog div,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog span,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog h1 {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog a {
    color: #5fb0e6 !important;
  }
  /* The CMP ships its own !important rules at higher specificity, so the
     headline, the footer "List of partners" link and the FAQ disc must be
     matched selector-for-selector or they stay black-on-dark / white. */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog .fc-header h1.fc-dialog-headline {
    color: #e6edf3 !important;
  }
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog .fc-footer a.fc-footer-link-v2,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog .fc-footer a.fc-footer-link-v2:visited {
    color: #5fb0e6 !important;
  }
  .fc-consent-root .fc-faq-header .fc-faq-icon {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    border-color: #2d333b !important;
  }
  .fc-consent-root .fc-faq-header .fc-faq-icon svg {
    fill: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  /* The compact "choice" dialog variant (.fc-choice-dialog, served on some
     visits instead of the full modal) frames its close button in a header
     strip painted rgba(255,255,255,.9) — a bright white bar across the top of
     the otherwise-dark dialog — and the close × sits on a white #fff cutout
     disc with a grey #5f6368 glyph. The first-dialog rules key on
     .fc-dialog-header / .fc-cutout defaults and never reach this variant. The
     CMP's own rules are .fc-consent-root .fc-choice-dialog-header /
     .fc-cutout-background (0,2,0 !important), so qualify one level deeper to win. */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-choice-dialog .fc-choice-dialog-header,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-close .fc-cutout-background {
    background-color: #1c2128 !important;
  }
  .fc-consent-root .fc-choice-dialog-header .fc-close svg {
    fill: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  /* The dialog's body copy is painted by the CMP's OWN high-specificity
     !important rules (e.g. `.fc-consent-root .fc-stacks .fc-stack-name` at
     0,3,0, `.fc-consent-root .fc-dialog .fc-footer p` at 0,4,0), which
     out-specify the broad `.fc-dialog span/p/div` lift above — so the purpose
     titles (#3c4043, ~1.2:1), the "Welcome"/"Manage your data" header text and
     the footer legal note (#5f6368, ~2:1) and the "Learn more" FAQ toggle
     stayed dark-on-dark on the "Manage options" preferences screen. Match each
     selector-for-selector, same as the headline/footer-link above. */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog .fc-stacks .fc-stack-name,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog .fc-header .fc-header-text,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-faq-header .fc-faq-label {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog .fc-footer p {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* Each TCF preference card is a white-bordered box (#dadce0) — light frames
     boxing the dark panels. The card body itself is already darkened by the
     .fc-preference-container entry in the bg block above; only the edge leaked. */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-preference-container {
    border-color: #2d333b !important;
  }
  /* The "Manage options" TCF preferences screen (.fc-data-preferences-dialog,
     reached from the consent dialog) is a deeper sub-surface the first-dialog
     rules never covered: its bare heading "Manage your data" is pure #000 (base
     rule, not .fc-dialog-headline), each purpose card title is #3c4043 (~1.2:1),
     and the descriptions / vendor-toggle labels are #5f6368. Match each at or
     above the CMP's own specificity (the h1 rule stays below the first dialog's
     0,4,0 headline rule, so that one keeps its brighter #e6edf3). */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-preferences-container .fc-preference-container .fc-preference-title h2,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-header h1,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog .fc-header h1 {
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
  }
  .fc-consent-root .fc-preference-container .fc-purpose-feature-description,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-preference-container .fc-preference-slider-label,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog-content .fc-preference-container .fc-preference-description,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog-content .fc-preference-container .fc-preference-description p,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog-content .fc-preference-container .fc-preference-description li,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog-content .fc-preference-container .fc-preference-description b,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-data-preferences-dialog .fc-body p {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* The "How this CMP works" explainer sits in .fc-noneditable-body, outside the
     preference cards, so the card-scoped rule above misses it. */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-data-preferences-dialog .fc-noneditable-body p,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-data-preferences-dialog .fc-noneditable-body li {
    color: #9aa3ad !important;
  }
  /* "View details" links live inside the description and are painted a dark
     #1967d2 (~3.3:1) by the CMP; lift to the accent blue. The manage-vendors
     nav button's label carries the same dark blue. */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-dialog-content .fc-preference-container .fc-preference-description a,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-navigation-button .fc-navigation-button-label {
    color: #5fb0e6 !important;
  }
  /* The manage-vendors / navigation buttons on the preferences screen ship a
     bare white fill with black text — darken to the neutral chip (the primary
     Accept-all / Confirm-choices CTAs keep their brand-blue fill). */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-data-preferences-dialog .fc-navigation-button {
    background-color: #21262d !important;
    color: #c4cdd6 !important;
    border-color: #2d333b !important;
  }
  .fc-consent-root .fc-footer-buttons-divider,
  .fc-consent-root .fc-preference-divider {
    background-color: #2d333b !important;
  }
  /* Re-assert the label on the brand-blue CTAs (the broad text rule
     above would otherwise dim them). */
  .fc-consent-root .fc-button .fc-button-label {
    color: #ffffff !important;
  }
}
